{"id": "2026-07-27-sports-pogacar-equals-all-time-tour-record", "date": "2026-07-27", "stream": "sports", "headline": "Pogacar equals all-time Tour record", "summary": "Tadej Pogacar won a record-equalling fifth Tour de France, drawing level with Anquetil, Merckx, Hinault and Indurain.", "url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/cycling/articles/c07r8d4d2z5o", "source_domain": "bbc.co.uk", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "Slovenia's Tadej Pogacar (UAE Team Emirates-XRG) sealed his fifth Tour de France on the Champs-Elysees, drawing level with the sport's four all-time greats - Jacques Anquetil, Eddy Merckx, Bernard Hinault and Miguel Indurain - as the only riders to win cycling's biggest race five times. It is his third in a row. As flagged here last week, the contest had effectively closed once his one real threat, two-time winner Jonas Vingegaard, abandoned with a broken collarbone on stage 15; his other rival, Belgium's Remco Evenepoel, finished second overall, 6 minutes 26 seconds back. Pogacar, 27, took five stage wins including a record ascent of Alpe d'Huez.", "why": "Five wins puts Pogacar in the conversation as the greatest cyclist ever - but the reception is telling. He was booed by some fans during the race, less out of dislike than frustration that his dominance has drained the Tour of suspense. That tension - a generational champion whose brilliance makes the event less competitive - is now the sport's central question.", "thread_id": "2026-07-27-sports-pogacar-equals-all-time-tour-record", "first_seen_date": "2026-07-27", "event_date": "2026-07-26", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Tadej Pogacar", "Tour de France", "Mathieu van der Poel", "Jonas Vingegaard", "Remco Evenepoel"]}
{"id": "2026-07-27-sports-norris-wins-as-antonelli-leads-title", "date": "2026-07-27", "stream": "sports", "headline": "Norris wins as Antonelli leads title", "summary": "Lando Norris took McLaren's first win of 2026 at the Hungarian GP as Piastri retired; Kimi Antonelli leads the championship into the summer break.", "url": "https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/f1-hungarian-gp-norris-wins-from-verstappen-and-antonelli-piastri-retires-with-gearbox-failure/10842087/", "source_domain": "autosport.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Lando Norris won the Hungarian Grand Prix for his and McLaren's first victory of the 2026 season - a striking line to write about a team that dominated the sport a year ago. His race-long McLaren team-mate Oscar Piastri led the first half after passing Norris at the start, but lost time trapped behind a Carlos Sainz-Fernando Alonso battle (Sainz got a five-second penalty for ignoring blue flags and drifting into Piastri, who raged over team radio), was overcut by Norris in the pits, then retired with a gearbox failure on lap 56. Max Verstappen salvaged second from a difficult weekend; Mercedes' teenager Kimi Antonelli took third after Lewis Hamilton was demoted by a pit-lane speeding penalty.", "why": "A year ago McLaren were the benchmark and Antonelli a rookie; that a Mercedes driver now leads by two clear wins' worth of points, and McLaren celebrated its first win only in late July, is the clearest sign yet that the 2026 regulation reset genuinely reshuffled the grid rather than merely tweaking it.", "thread_id": "2026-07-27-sports-norris-wins-as-antonelli-leads-title", "first_seen_date": "2026-07-27", "event_date": "2026-07-26", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Lando Norris", "McLaren", "Oscar Piastri", "Kimi Antonelli", "Max Verstappen", "Lewis Hamilton", "Mercedes", "Hungarian Grand Prix"]}
{"id": "2026-07-27-sports-swiss-super-league-season-opens", "date": "2026-07-27", "stream": "sports", "headline": "Swiss Super League season opens", "summary": "The 2026-27 Swiss Super League began, St. Gallen beating FCZ 2-1 and Young Boys beating Sion 4-2, both after conceding first.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/sport/fussball/super-league/super-league-1-spieltag-st-galler-doppelschlag-zieht-dem-fcz-den-stecker", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The 2026-27 Swiss Super League - the country's twelve-team top flight - kicked off this weekend, and the two marquee Sunday fixtures both turned on late comebacks. In front of a sold-out St. Gallen, the hosts trailed to a first-half Umeh Emmanuel goal for Zurich before Lukas Goertler equalised from a worked corner (70') and summer signing Andrin Hunziker deflected in the winner four minutes later for a 2-1 St. Gallen victory. It was a pointed result for FCZ's new coach Marcel Koller - the man who led St. Gallen to their last league title 26 years ago - whose reshaped side created the better first-half chances but left empty-handed. In Bern, Young Boys threw away a 2-0 lead against Sion before Samuel Essende's second-half brace rescued a 4-2 win.", "why": "For most Swiss towns the Super League - not the World Cup that just finished - is the sport that structures the autumn, and the opening weekend already hints at the season's shape: a champion (Thun) nobody expected to defend, a rebuilt Zurich under a returning veteran coach, and a St. Gallen side punching above its weight at home and in Europe.", "thread_id": "2026-07-27-sports-swiss-super-league-season-opens", "first_seen_date": "2026-07-27", "event_date": "2026-07-26", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["St. Gallen", "FC Zurich", "Young Boys", "Sion", "Swiss Super League", "Thun", "Marcel Koller"]}
{"id": "2026-07-27-sports-tagger-and-halys-land-maiden-titles", "date": "2026-07-27", "stream": "sports", "headline": "Tagger and Halys land maiden titles", "summary": "Austrian teenager Lilli Tagger won her first WTA title in Prague and France's Quentin Halys his first ATP title in Kitzbuehel.", "url": "https://www.wtatennis.com/news/4546947/teenager-tagger-captures-maiden-wta-singles-title-in-prague", "source_domain": "wtatennis.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["via-snippet"], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "The post-Wimbledon lull is a quiet, lower-tier stretch of the calendar, but this week delivered two genuine breakthroughs. Austrian teenager Lilli Tagger won the WTA Prague Open for her first career title on the women's tour, beating Ukraine's Daria Snigur 7-6(3), 6-2 on Sunday. A day earlier, France's Quentin Halys took the ATP Generali Open in Kitzbuehel - his maiden ATP Tour title - edging Alexander Bublik 6-4, 7-6(8-6). Neither event carries ranking weight near the top of the game, and there was no Swiss winner this week.", "why": "First titles are the tour's leading indicator - they mark which unseeded names are about to start troubling the seeds at the bigger hard-court events (Canada, Cincinnati, then the US Open) over the next month.", "thread_id": "2026-07-27-sports-tagger-and-halys-land-maiden-titles", "first_seen_date": "2026-07-27", "event_date": "2026-07-26", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Lilli Tagger", "Quentin Halys", "WTA Prague Open", "ATP Kitzbuehel", "Daria Snigur", "Alexander Bublik"]}
